# winoracle 2026-09-28, WARP, FL 11_1, x64 (x86 identical). Vitreo verdicts:
#  R1 cull x front x fill, NULL state, IsFrontFace for lines/points/wireframe: CORRECT
#  R2 viewport transform, pixel centre, SV_Position.w, zero-size/unset viewport: CORRECT
#  R2 MinDepth > MaxDepth: WRONG (Windows skips the RSSetViewports call,
#     spec 15.6.1; Vitreo binds it and inverts depth)
#  R3 scissor with no rect set: WRONG (Windows: nothing, default rect is
#     {0,0,0,0}; Vitreo: scissor off). Inverted rect: WRONG (Vitreo draws
#     all). Negative left/top: WRONG (Vitreo draws nothing; Windows clamps)
#  R3 implicit viewport scissor incl. fractional origin: CORRECT
#  R4 D24S8 DepthBias: WRONG (float r = 2^(exp(z)-23) used for a UNORM
#     buffer: bias halves for z<0.5); D16: within 1-2 units (minor);
#     D32/D32S8 constant+slope+clamp, line no-bias, wireframe bias: CORRECT
#  R5 DepthClipEnable, viewport depth clamp: CORRECT. SV_Depth with
#     DepthClip on: WRONG (not clamped to MinDepth/MaxDepth, spec 15.6)
#     (D16 0.25 clear reads 0x3FFF: ClearDepthStencilView rounding, area 06)
#  R6 top-left rule, 16.8 snapping, slivers: CORRECT
#  R7 aliased lines, points, wireframe: CORRECT. Alpha-AA lines
#     (AntialiasedLineEnable) and quadrilateral lines (MultisampleEnable):
#     MISSING (drawn aliased)
#  R8 4x coverage per sample (quality 0): CORRECT; quality
#     D3D11_STANDARD_MULTISAMPLE_PATTERN: create E_INVALIDARG (area 01/02)
